{"name":"Aviary Blue","hex":"#c6e3e8","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aviary","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A house, enclosure, large cage, or other place for keeping birds confined; a birdhouse. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aviary"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aviary","blocks":[{"text":"An aviary is a large enclosure for confining birds, although bats may also be considered for display. Unlike birdcages, aviaries allow birds a larger living space where they can fly; hence, aviaries are also sometimes known as flight cages in the United Kingdom. Aviaries often contain plants and shrubbery to simulate a natural environment."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Aviary_N%C3%A9then.jpg/330px-Aviary_N%C3%A9then.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aviary","wikidata":"Q1363025"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/A_Bali_Starling_or_Rothschild_Mynah_at_the_Waddesdon_Aviary.jpg/500px-A_Bali_Starling_or_Rothschild_Mynah_at_the_Waddesdon_Aviary.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/A_Bali_Starling_or_Rothschild_Mynah_at_the_Waddesdon_Aviary.jpg/1280px-A_Bali_Starling_or_Rothschild_Mynah_at_the_Waddesdon_Aviary.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/A_Bali_Starling_or_Rothschild_Mynah_at_the_Waddesdon_Aviary.jpg/500px-A_Bali_Starling_or_Rothschild_Mynah_at_the_Waddesdon_Aviary.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Bali Myna, otherwise known as the Rothschild Myna, is one of the seven EAZA species at Waddesdon Manor's Aviary in Buckinghamshire, UK.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_Bali_Starling_or_Rothschild_Mynah_at_the_Waddesdon_Aviary.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/43/Military_aviary2.jpg/500px-Military_aviary2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/43/Military_aviary2.jpg/1280px-Military_aviary2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/43/Military_aviary2.jpg/500px-Military_aviary2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Proposed ar